 "title": "Downstream fix: Hash API token secrets with single-pass SHA-256 instead of hashSecret",
 "description": "@AlphaTechini asked for option 1 in #6. Option: Hash API token secrets with a fast single-pass SHA-256 instead of hashSecret in issueToken and verifyToken, since token secrets are long random values, and keep the higher iteration count only for passwords; this leaves token secrets without key stretching, which is acceptable only because they are random. Downstream committed it and will re-measure the journey from the issue on this merge request. Review it before merging; Downstream never merges.",
